extends RefCounted

# Hand-drawn rooms that world_gen.gd assembles into a world per seed. One
# grid cell is 32 x 18 tiles of 40 px (1280 x 720, one screen); the arena
# is two cells wide. Doors sit at fixed places so any two rooms line up:
#   L / R  rows 12-15 of the outer column (floor at row 16)
#   U      columns 12-19 of row 0, over a ledge at row 2 (leave by its
#          middle, columns 14-17, under the drop-through above)
#   D      columns 14-17 of rows 16-17, covered by a drop-through ledge
# Every room is drawn with all the doors it supports open; the builder
# walls up the ones a seed doesn't use. A room's doors must all be
# reachable from each other with a plain jump (world_gen.gd checks), except
# where a room is a gate by design.
#
#   #  bedrock          =  ledge (jump up through, Down + Jump to drop)
#   E  earth (diggable) R  rock (needs a bronze pickaxe)
#   c  copper in earth  t  tin in earth     f  flint in earth
#   x  ember pit (hurts, and puts Veyl back on solid ground)
#   b  branch           k  flint stone      S  ember shrine
#   m  Mossling         w  Ember Wolf       a  Ashcrawler
#   X  the Cinderwing   H  an Ember Heart   N  Rowan   B  the Ashbound

